| F1 | open | BLOCKING | js/common/mergeBackstop.js | 🚨 blocking ci red at head bf94b523 — the crap ratchet fails exit 2 the crap check fails on this pr s head commit ci failures md ci failures md run 42795874525 full log in ci failures full log text crap ratchet regression js unit tests test mergebot js fixture 11 12 new 8 js common mergebackstop js commentsforrun 9 2 1 regression s 1 new over threshold 0 improvement s 0 removed the ratchet is monotone crap may only decrease so commentsforrun — introduced by this hunk — must land at crap ≤ 8 and the test mergebot js fixture must come back to 11 two concrete remediation paths 1 commentsforrun 9 2 — the two fail closed throw branches are never exercised the iofixture in test mergebackstop js always provides getcomments so the t prcomments → return null path and the comments needsledger → throw path stay uncovered either a add the two negative tests — a hold only run without a comments primitive returns null an ack counted run without one or with a null read throws — which lifts the coverage term below the gate or b extract the throw into a named helper e g requireledgerbase t cls inp which drops the branch count under the ceiling 2 test mergebot js fixture 11 → 12 — the 1 decision is the new opts prcomments default inside the github get pr comments mock test mergebot js 262 normalize the default outside the bag literal or hoist it into a tiny helper to restore cc 11 everything else is green ci shows 9416 tests passed 0 failed and a local re run of the six touched suites totals 372 passed 0 failed — only the measured complexity gate is red per the repo s gate doctrine a failing measured gate is ci breakage and blocks the merge |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/mergeBackstop.js | 💡 suggestion the clean replay branch cannot resolve acks — the call below this line is a provable no op openmachinecount cls counted length ackthreads length holdthreads length and ackthreads are a subset of the open machine rows every ack thread row bumps openmachinecount via classifyrow → bucketbelowthresholdrow so when openmachinecount cls is true cls ackthreads is always and the resolveackthreads t inp prnumber cls ackthreads out on the next line iterates nothing the live ack path is the shared tail after ledgerphase mergebackstop js 1070 — which is what the gh 1418 tests actually exercise ac2 ac3 assert the ledger stamp and the resolves on that path this branch is the pre gh 1418 leftover the old condition was cls counted length under which the call did work the comment above it still reads deferrable tier machine threads resolve the wontfix ack path each with its ledger item — which cannot happen in this branch suggest deleting the dead call and re wording the comment to name the branch what it now is the pure clean replay zero open machine threads → merge proceeds keeping the current comment invites a future editor to fix the condition back to cls counted length which would silently skip the ledger phase for ack only runs — the exact gh 1352 invariant this pr adds behavior is unchanged either way 81 81 test mergebackstop tests pass so this is clarity not correctness |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

